    {
      "id": "sol.amc-8-2008-p22.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(x=\\dfrac{n}{3}\\). Then \\(n=3x\\), so \\(3n=9x\\).\n\nBoth \\(x\\) and \\(9x\\) must be three-digit whole numbers. Thus \\(100\\le x\\) and \\(9x\\le999\\), so \\(100\\le x\\le111\\).\n\nThere are \\(111-100+1=12\\) integer values of \\(x\\), and each gives one positive integer value of \\(n\\).\n\nThus, A is the correct answer.",
